  "decision_rules": [
    "A pressure is graph-specific only if its selected model or chunk entered through a graph/expansion source or if its graph target model was unavailable from direct anchors, frame routes, structural gaps, and recorded embeddings.",
    "Model availability is not answer simulation and does not prove that another pathway would write the same challenge.",
    "If no admitted pressure is graph-specific at the recorded handoff, Case 10 cannot authorize a paid graph ablation.",
    "If graph expansion was unconsumed, graph-disabled and shuffled-edge comparisons are non-identifying no-ops rather than negative evidence about graph quality.",
    "No output may claim that graph expansion is useless in other cases."
  ],
